From 778f74b560ad541085d6cee48e29c4a45bad7956 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:12:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] macos-arm64: UI scale for HiDPI, multi-display native
 modes

- vgui surface: vgui_scale (0 = auto: render pixels per window point);
  applied to the 2D projection, screen size, cursor and mouse events, the
  engine's UI-size root panels, and the client's mouse recentering.
- display info reports real pixel sizes; native mode clamping uses the
  largest display's pixel size; mode list is the union of all displays.
---
